    "description": "Fuluhashi EPO Corporation engages in the processing and recycling of wood waste in Japan. The company operates through Biomaterials, Resource recycling, and other businesses. It is involved in the processing of wood waste; sale of wood chips; recycling of construction by-products; and manufacturing, procurement, and sale of logistics equipment, and wooden pallets. It also engages in the wood biomass power generation business; environmental logistics business; and vacant house management and support business. The company was formerly known as FULUHASHI CORPORATION and changed its name to Fuluhashi Epo Corporation in April 2008. Fuluhashi Epo Corporation was founded in 1947 and is headquartered in Nagoya, Japan."
